2026-10-04T18:54:59.6932260Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-04T18:54:59.6990530Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-04T18:54:59.6992840Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-04T18:54:59.6993730Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-04T18:54:59.6994150Z 
2026-10-04T18:54:59.6995530Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-04T18:54:59.6996000Z 
2026-10-04T18:54:59.6996410Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-04T18:54:59.6997260Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-04T18:54:59.6997700Z 
2026-10-04T18:54:59.6997930Z If you would like to
2026-10-04T18:54:59.6998440Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-04T18:54:59.6998820Z 
2026-10-04T18:54:59.6999150Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-04T18:54:59.6999890Z   $ sh ./install-nix
